1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,210
Patrick, thanks so much for looking after Courtney.

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,820
Dorsia. How impressive.

3
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:07,980
How on Earth did you get a reservation there?

4
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:08,970
Lucky, I guess.

5
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:12,410
That's a wonderful suit.

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,030
Don't tell me. Don't tell me. Let me guess.

7
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,690
Mmm, Valentino Couture?

8
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:18,970
Uh-huh. Hmm.

9
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:21,030
It looks so soft.

10
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:23,630
Your compliment was sufficient, Luis.

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:29,580
Hello, Halberstram. Nice tie. How the hell are you?

12
00:00:29,490 --> 00:00:32,290
Allen has mistaken me for this dickhead, Marcus Halberstram.

13
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:35,550
It seems logical, because Marcus also works at P&P...

14
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:38,160
and in fact does the same exact thing I do.

15
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:41,040
He also has a penchant for Valentino suits...

16
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:42,550
and Oliver Peoples glasses.

17
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:44,480
Marcus and I even go to the same barber...

18
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,320
although I have a slightly better haircut.

19
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:48,790
So, how's the Ransom account going, Marcus?

20
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,130
It's, uh, it's all right.

21
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:53,100
Really? That's interesting. It's not, uh, not great.

22
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:55,160
Oh, well, you know... So, how's Cecilia?

23
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,450
She's a great girl. Oh, yeah. I'm very lucky.

24
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:01,840
Hey, Allen, congratulations on the Fisher account.

25
00:01:01,370 --> 00:01:05,110
Thank you, Baxter. Listen, Paul. Squash.

26
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:12,520
Call me. How about Friday?

27
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:15,960
No can do. I got an 8:30 res at Dorsia.

28
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:16,670
Great sea urchin ceviche.

29
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:23,070
Dorsia on Friday night? How'd he swing that?

30
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:24,070
I think he's lying.

31
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,960
Is that a gram? New card.

32
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,960
What do you think?

33
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:36,040
Whoa-ho. Very nice.

34
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:37,720
Look at that.

35
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,120
Picked them up from the printer's, yesterday.

36
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:43,320
Good coloring. That's bone.

37
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,260
And the lettering is something called Silian Rail.

38
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:48,800
It's very cool, Bateman, but that's nothing. Look at this.

39
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:50,620
That is really nice.

40
00:01:50,530 --> 00:01:54,740
Eggshell with Romalian type. What do you think?

41
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:56,860
Nice.

42
00:01:57,420 --> 00:02:00,350
Jesus. That is really super.

43
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:03,810
How a nitwit like you get so tasteful?

44
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:05,110
I can't believe that Bryce...

45
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,260
prefers Van Patten's card to mine.

46
00:02:07,590 --> 00:02:11,320
But wait. You ain't seen nothin' yet.

47
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:16,650
Raised lettering, pale nimbus, white.

48
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,560
Impressive. Very nice.

49
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:21,210
Hmm.

50
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:24,660
Let's see Paul Allen's card.

51
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:41,840
Look at that subtle off-white coloring.

52
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:44,800
The tasteful thickness of it.

53
00:02:43,210 --> 00:02:47,690
Oh, my God. It even has a watermark.

54
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:54,420
Is something wrong, Patrick?

55
00:02:54,910 --> 00:02:55,990
You're sweating.
